{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Then were they alarmed, etc.</b> The verse's saying ״אָז״ ('then') is to say that it does not refer to the time He has been speaking of until now, which is the time of those entering the Land, but rather to the time of the coming of our redeemer. Therefore it says ״אָז נִבְהֲלוּ אַלּוּפֵי אֱדוֹם״ ('then the chiefs of Edom were alarmed'); and so it says (Numbers 24:18) ״וְהָיָה אֱדוֹם יְרֵשָׁה״, and then too the time will arrive to merit Moab and Ammon. Therefore it says <b>the chiefs of Moab shall trembling seize them</b>. And the reason it did not mention Ammon is that it too comes from a father — meaning, together with his daughter — and then too we shall merit all the rest of the Canaanite nations, which is what it means by saying ״נָמֹגוּ כֹּל יֹשְׁבֵי כְנָעַן״ ('all the inhabitants of Canaan melted away'). And it says <b>inhabitants</b> to say that through them even the rest of the nations will be purified. And the reason it speaks in the past tense is that the word of HaShem is as though it were already fulfilled and done."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:28.270797531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}